Microsoft is set to drop OneDrive support for iOS 18 and iPadOS 18, which will remove the cloud storage app's compatibility with several older iPhones and one iPad model.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/microsoft-onedrive-logo@2x-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="2560" height="1440" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1068894" /><br/>
The loss of support for iOS 18 will impact the iPhone XR, iPhone XS, and iPhone XS Max, because these devices can't be updated to iOS 26. Likewise, the seventh-generation iPad will be left behind when Microsoft raises the app's minimum requirement to iPadOS 26.<br/>
<br/>
OneDrive 18.12.1 is the final version to support iOS 18 and iPadOS 18, based on release notes for Microsoft's latest TestFlight beta. <br/>
<br/>
It's not clear when the change will translate to the public version of OneDrive. That said, Microsoft recently added a notice to its <a href="https://apps.apple.com/app/microsoft-onedrive/id477537958">App Store listing</a> saying that support for iOS and iPadOS 18 will be dropped "soon," and recommending that users update to iOS 26 or iOS 27 to continue receiving the latest versions.<br/>
<br/>
